  const noSummaryDiv = document.createElement('div');
  noSummaryDiv.className = 'call-summary empty';
  noSummaryDiv.textContent = 'No summary';
  card.appendChild(noSummaryDiv);
}

listContainer.appendChild(card);
if (toggleCheck) toggleCheck();
```

Then delete the old `listContainer.appendChild(card);` that follows this block, since the new code already appends the card.

## Why this works
- The text is clamped to 3 lines, but the button lives outside the clamped element, so it's never clipped.
- The button appears only when the text really overflows, so short summaries like "Booked a follow-up for Friday." don't get a useless "Read more". This replaces the old `length > 180` guess.
- The button is now 44px tall for phone tapping and keeps its `aria-expanded` state.

## One more fix
In the `<meta name="viewport">` tag, remove `maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no`. It blocks pinch-zoom, which hurts accessibility, and it isn't needed because your inputs are already 16px, which prevents the iOS auto-zoom.



